# N, THE INDUCTION MATRIX: a commitment made here that becomes a draw somewhere else, and
# who made it. Same shape as D, different fact, hence a different relation.
#
# ⭐⭐ ONLY AN INDUCTION NAMES A DECIDER, and that is the point of separating the two. A draw
#    is a thing that occurred; an induction is a thing somebody CHOSE, creating a future
#    draw on a different supply. Folding them into one table with a flag would have put an
#    event and a decision in one slot.
-- pm:Operation/pm:Induction, carrying pm:decidedBy.
SELECT n.filing, n.operation, n.layer,
       n.low, n.mode, n.high, n.unit, n.absent, n.decider
FROM pm.induction n
